DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection in h2o HTTP server. Three core flags
  (--exec-mode, --exec-verbose, --exec-debug) must all be present as checked
  by exec_config_ok(). The command flows through an exec_args_t struct into
  dispatch_exec() which calls system(). An optional fourth flag --exec-strict
  enables semicolon blocking; bypass is to omit it.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — three flags + utility function):
  mechanism:  Three core CLI flags stored in global struct exec_cfg
              { int enabled; int verbose; int debug; int strict; }
  check:      exec_config_ok() returns enabled && verbose && debug
  complexity: one struct, three required flags, one utility function,
              plus an optional fourth field for S3 sanitization gating

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  req->path (set by HTTP parser)
  path:       exec_handler_on_req() extracts cmd via memcmp/offset arithmetic
              cmd placed into exec_args_t { const char *cmd; size_t len; int flags; }
              exec_args_t passed to dispatch_exec() which calls snprintf+system
  transforms: one level of struct indirection before reaching system()

SANITIZATION (S3 — flag-gated check):
  check:      if exec_cfg.strict is set, reject commands containing semicolons
  bypass:     omit --exec-strict flag → semicolon check never performed
  note:       exploit works with --exec-mode --exec-verbose --exec-debug (no --exec-strict)

SINK:        system(buf) in dispatch_exec() (src/main.c)

